  "headline": "The Pink City",
  "short_description": "Rajasthan's capital is famed for its rose-pink old city, hilltop forts and royal Rajput heritage.",
  "about": "Founded in 1727 by Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II, Jaipur is part of India's Golden Triangle and a showcase of Rajput architecture and urban planning.\n\nLocated in eastern Rajasthan, surrounded by the Aravalli hills.\n\nFamous for block-print textiles, blue pottery, gemstone jewellery and Rajasthani folk music and dance.\n\nPredominantly Hindu, with significant Jain heritage reflected in temples across the state.",
  "history": "Purpose-built as a planned city in the 18th century, later painted pink to welcome the Prince of Wales in 1876, giving it its nickname.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Jaipur International Airport (airport)\n- Jaipur Junction (railway)\n- Sindhi Camp Bus Stand (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Hindi, Rajasthani, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to March",
  "ideal_duration_text": "2–3 days",
  "nearest_airport": "Jaipur International Airport (JAI)",
  "nearest_railway_station": "Jaipur Junction",
